<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60461" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυᾰνο-χαίτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dark-haired</i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> usu. of Poseidon, perh. in reference to the <i>dark
			blue</i> of the sea, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				20.144
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.536
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				278
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρείων</span> Thebais <i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>; of a horse, <i>dark-maned</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				20.224
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				120
			</span></i>: voc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυανοχαῖτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Cer.</u>
					347
				</span></i>
			:—also nom. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυανοχαῖτα</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.563
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				14.390
			</span></i>; treated as indeclin. and joined with dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυανοχαῖτα Ποσειδάωνι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antim.
					27
				</span></i>
			. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span>, metri
		gr.]</div>
